A copy of that license is in LICENSE-FISH-AUDIO. The Fish Audio Materials were
changed as follows:

- speak_as_you_think/encode.py: encode_segments() follows the row-encoding loop of
  build_drama3_prompt() in fish_speech/models/text2semantic/fish_omni/generate.py.
  It takes a list of segments and checks the shape of the codes.
- speak_as_you_think/prompts.py: the prompt literals (message markers, the
  text-to-speech instruction, the reference block) equal those in
  fish_omni/generate.py, so that prompts tokenize the same way. The streaming
  rounds are new.
- speak_as_you_think/chunker.py: the sentence and clause marks and the protected-span
  loop follow fish_omni/chunking.py. Splitting by minimum and maximum characters
  is new.
- experiments/week1_run.py: reference_text() is taken from tools/tts_sample.py.

Everything else in this repository is the author's own work. No model weights
are included.
